From: Neil Horman <nhorman@openssl.org>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:49:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix set but unsued variable in lib/opt.c

https://github.com/openssl/openssl/actions/runs/34494520852/job/102982686286

CI is failing because we have a varaible in opt.c that is set but never
used.

Just remove it.

Reviewed-by: Andrew Dinh <andrewd@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Frederik Wedel-Heinen <fwh.openssl@gmail.com>
MergeDate: Sat Sep 12 13:18:16 2026
Reviewed-by: Mounir Idrassi <mounir.idrassi@idrix.fr>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33194
(cherry picked from commit eadfce0e20dafd9a9bc8232caf84c4c9498ea667)
---
 apps/lib/opt.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/apps/lib/opt.c b/apps/lib/opt.c
index f9135f4549be..9b613ef63d31 100644
--- a/apps/lib/opt.c
+++ b/apps/lib/opt.c
@@ -36,7 +36,6 @@ const char OPT_PARAM_STR[] = "-P";
 
 /* Our state */
 static char **argv;
-static int argc;
 static int opt_index;
 static char *arg;
 static char *flag;
@@ -161,7 +160,6 @@ char *opt_getprog(void)
 char *opt_init(int ac, char **av, const OPTIONS *o)
 {
     /* Store state. */
-    argc = ac;
     argv = av;
     opt_begin();
     opts = o;
